.TH NFTBAN 1 "November 2025" "nftban v0.32.26" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nftban \- Simplifying Linux Firewall Management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nftban
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nftban
is a modern Linux firewall management system that combines nftables and fail2ban
to provide comprehensive network security. It offers an intuitive CLI for managing
bans, whitelists, threat feeds, GeoBan country blocking, and health monitoring.

NFTBan v0.32.26 uses a dual-table architecture with inet family for unified IPv4/IPv6 management,
providing 10-60x performance improvements through Go-powered atomic operations and feed processing.

.SH QUICKSTART
Just installed NFTBan and don't know what to do? Run this command:
.RS
.B nftban setup
.RE

This interactive wizard will:
.RS
.TP
• Fix all permissions and directories
.TP
• Verify system health
.TP
• Optionally enable the firewall
.TP
• Guide you step-by-step through setup
.RE

For non-interactive (automated) setup:
.RS
.B nftban setup \-\-auto
.RE

After setup completes, check your firewall status:
.RS
.B nftban status
.RE

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information for the command
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-interactive
Disable interactive prompts (for scripting)
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output results in JSON format

.SH COMMANDS
.SS Setup & Configuration
.TP
.B setup
Interactive first-time setup wizard (recommended for new installations)
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Non-interactive mode (skip all prompts)
.TP
.B Example:
nftban setup
.br
nftban setup \-\-auto
.RE

.SS Ban Management
.TP
.B ban \fIIP\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Ban an IP address permanently or temporarily
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-temp
Create temporary ban
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
Ban duration for temporary bans (default: 3600)
.TP
.B \-\-reason \fIREASON\fR
Reason for the ban (logged in audit)
.RE

.TP
.B unban \fIIP\fR
Remove ban for an IP address
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Remove from all ban lists (permanent, temp, fail2ban)
.RE

.TP
.B search \fIIP\fR
Search for IP in all nftables sets and fail2ban jails
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-interactive
Non-interactive output for scripting
.RE

.SS Whitelist Management
.TP
.B whitelist add \fIIP\fR
Add IP to permanent whitelist (never blocked)

.TP
.B whitelist remove \fIIP\fR
Remove IP from whitelist

.TP
.B whitelist list
Show all whitelisted IPs

.SS Feed Management
.TP
.B feeds list
List all available threat intelligence feeds

.TP
.B feeds enable \fIFEED\fR
Enable a threat feed (e.g., greensnow, cloudflare)

.TP
.B feeds disable \fIFEED\fR
Disable a threat feed

.TP
.B feeds update
Update all enabled feeds (downloads latest threat IPs)
.RS
Uses atomic loader (nftban-feeds) for 5-15x faster processing.
Supports ETag caching, CIDR merging, and intelligent delta limiting.
.RE

.TP
.B feeds load
Load feed IPs into nftables sets atomically

.TP
.B feeds version
Show nftban-feeds binary version and build information

.SS Port Management
.TP
.B port add \fIPORT\fR [\fIPROTOCOL\fR]
Add port to allowed services (zero-downtime atomic operation)
.RS
.TP
.B PROTOCOL
both (default, safest - allows TCP+UDP), tcp, or udp
.TP
.B Examples:
nftban port add 8080        # TCP+UDP (default, safest)
.br
nftban port add 443 tcp     # TCP only
.br
nftban port add 53 udp      # UDP only
.RE

.TP
.B port remove \fIPORT\fR [\fIPROTOCOL\fR]
Remove port from allowed services (zero-downtime atomic operation)
.RS
System ports (00-*.conf) are protected from accidental removal.
.RE

.TP
.B port search \fIPORT\fR
Search for port in nftables sets and configuration files
.RS
Shows if port is currently active in nftables and which config files reference it.
.RE

.TP
.B port block \fIPORT\fR
Block a port (TCP+UDP on IPv4+IPv6)
.RS
Removes port from whitelist, blocking all traffic. Protected against blocking active SSH port.
.TP
.B Example:
nftban port block 3389        # Block RDP port
.RE

.TP
.B port unblock \fIPORT\fR
Unblock a port (TCP+UDP on IPv4+IPv6)
.RS
Adds port to whitelist, allowing traffic on both TCP and UDP protocols.
.TP
.B Example:
nftban port unblock 8080      # Allow port 8080
.RE

.SS GeoBan Management (Country Blocking)
.TP
.B geoban ban \fICOUNTRY_CODE\fR
Ban all traffic from a country (e.g., CN, RU)
.RS
Atomically blocks all IPs from the specified country using nftables netlink.
Creates configuration file in /etc/nftban/geoban.d/50-ban-XX.conf
.RE

.TP
.B geoban unban \fICOUNTRY_CODE\fR
Remove country ban and unload IPs from nftables
.RS
Atomically removes all country IPs from nftables sets and deletes config file.
.RE

.TP
.B geoban whitelist \fICOUNTRY_CODE\fR
Whitelist a country (never blocked, even if banned)
.RS
Creates configuration file in /etc/nftban/geoban.d/40-whitelist-XX.conf
Takes precedence over bans.
.RE

.TP
.B geoban unwhitelist \fICOUNTRY_CODE\fR
Remove country from whitelist

.TP
.B geoban list
List all banned and whitelisted countries with IP counts

.TP
.B geoban refresh \fICOUNTRY_CODE\fR
Refresh IP list for a country (re-download from RIR sources)

.TP
.B geoban config
Show current GeoBan configuration and statistics

.SS GeoIP Database Management
.TP
.B geoip lookup \fIIP\fR [\fIFORMAT\fR]
Lookup country code for an IP address using MaxMind GeoLite2
.RS
Formats: json (default), compact, country
.RE

.TP
.B geoip bulk \fIFILE\fR
Bulk lookup of multiple IPs from file or stdin

.TP
.B geoip status
Show GeoIP database status and configuration

.TP
.B geoip update
Download or update the GeoIP database

.TP
.B geoip test
Run GeoIP system tests

.TP
.B geoip config \fICOMMAND\fR
Configure GeoIP database settings
.RS
.TP
.B show
Display current configuration
.TP
.B set-source \fISOURCE\fR
Set database source (github or maxmind)
.TP
.B set-key \fIKEY\fR
Set MaxMind license key
.TP
.B test-download
Test database download
.RE

.TP
.B geoip version
Show nftban-geoip binary version and build information

.SS Health & Monitoring
.TP
.B health check
Run comprehensive system health check
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-heal
Automatically fix detected issues (requires permissions)
.RE

.TP
.B stats
Display ban statistics and system metrics
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-summary
Show summary statistics only
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format
.RE

.TP
.B report generate
Generate detailed security report
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIFORMAT\fR
Report format: text, json, html (default: text)
.TP
.B \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Save report to file
.RE

.SS Service Management
.TP
.B start \fISERVICE\fR
Start nftables or fail2ban service

.TP
.B stop \fISERVICE\fR
Stop nftables or fail2ban service

.TP
.B restart \fISERVICE\fR
Restart nftables or fail2ban service

.TP
.B enable \fISERVICE\fR
Enable service to start on boot

.TP
.B disable \fISERVICE\fR
Disable service from starting on boot

.TP
.B status \fISERVICE\fR
Show service status

.SS Permission Management
.TP
.B permissions check
Check all file/directory permissions against FHS specification

.TP
.B permissions enforce
Fix incorrect permissions (requires root or nftban-cli group)

.SS Mail Integration
.TP
.B mail enable
Enable email notifications for security events

.TP
.B mail disable
Disable email notifications

.TP
.B mail test
Send test email to verify configuration

.SS Fail2ban Integration
.TP
.B fail2ban status
Show fail2ban status and statistics

.TP
.B fail2ban jails
List all jails (enabled and disabled) with their status
.RS
Shows all available NFTBan fail2ban jails, marking which are enabled
(✓ active) and which are disabled, along with banned IP counts for
active jails. Users can select jails to enable or disable.
.RE

.TP
.B fail2ban available
Show all available jails on this system

.TP
.B fail2ban auto-discovery [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Scan system for installed services and show compatible jails
.RS
Automatically detects which NFTBan jails are compatible with your system
by checking for required services and log files. Shows three categories:
already enabled jails, compatible jails ready to enable, and incompatible
jails (service not found).
.TP
.B \-\-enable
Automatically enable all discovered compatible jails
.RE

.TP
.B fail2ban jail \fINAME\fR
Show detailed status for specific jail

.TP
.B fail2ban enable \fIJAIL\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Enable/start a fail2ban jail
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Force enable even if requirements are not met (not recommended)
.RE

.TP
.B fail2ban disable \fIJAIL\fR
Disable/stop a fail2ban jail

.TP
.B fail2ban banned [\fIJAIL\fR]
List banned IPs (all jails or specific)

.TP
.B fail2ban ban \fIJAIL\fR \fIIP\fR
Manually ban an IP in a jail

.TP
.B fail2ban unban \fIJAIL\fR \fIIP\fR
Unban an IP from a jail

.TP
.B fail2ban health-fix [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Check and auto-fix jail configuration problems
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-save-report [\fIFILE\fR]
Save health check report to file (default: /var/log/nftban/reports/fail2ban-health-TIMESTAMP.txt)
.TP
.B \-\-mail \fIEMAIL\fR
Send health check report via email
.RE

.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B /etc/nftban/nftban.conf
Main configuration file

.TP
.B /etc/nftban/conf.d/*.conf
Modular configuration files:
.RS
.TP
.I feeds.conf
Threat feed settings
.TP
.I nftban-go.conf
Go binary settings (CPU/RAM limits, safety thresholds)
.TP
.I mail.conf
Email notification settings
.TP
.I banner.conf
Banner display and update check settings
.RE

.TP
.B /etc/nftban/geoban.d/
GeoBan country configuration directory:
.RS
.TP
.I 40-whitelist-*.conf
Whitelisted countries (never blocked)
.TP
.I 50-ban-*.conf
Banned countries (all IPs blocked)
.RE

.SS Update Notifications
NFTBan can automatically check for new versions and display a notification banner when updates are available.

.TP
.B How It Works
.RS
.TP
• Checks GitHub API for latest release (github.com/itcmsgr/nftban)
.TP
• Runs once per 24 hours (configurable cache TTL)
.TP
• 3-second timeout to prevent blocking if GitHub is unreachable
.TP
• Compares semantic versions (X.Y.Z)
.TP
• Shows yellow notification box in banner when update available
.TP
• Disabled by default for privacy (no automatic network calls)
.RE

.TP
.B Enable Update Check
Edit /etc/nftban/conf.d/banner.conf and set:
.RS
.B NFTBAN_BANNER_UPDATE_CHECK="true"
.RE

.TP
.B Configuration Options
.RS
.TP
.B NFTBAN_BANNER_UPDATE_CHECK
Enable/disable update checking (default: false)
.TP
.B NFTBAN_REPO
GitHub repository for update check (default: "itcmsgr/nftban")
.TP
.B NFTBAN_UPDATE_TTL
Cache duration in seconds (default: 86400 = 24 hours)
.RE

.TP
.B Example Notification
When a new version is available, users see:
.RS
.nf
╭────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│  📦 Update Available: v0.33.0                              │
│  Current: v0.32.26                                         │
│  Download: github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/releases             │
╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
.fi
.RE

.TP
.B Privacy & Performance
.RS
• Disabled by default - no automatic network calls
.TP
• When enabled, checks only once per 24 hours
.TP
• 3-second timeout prevents CLI delays
.TP
• Results cached in /var/cache/nftban/update_check
.TP
• Non-blocking - CLI works even if GitHub unreachable
.RE

