.SH ARCHITECTURE
NFTBan uses a modern dual-table architecture:

.TP
.B inet nftban_main
Main persistent table with priority -10 (processed first)
.RS
Contains: whitelist, permanent bans, feeds, GeoIP blocks
.RE

.TP
.B inet nftban_runtime
Runtime table with priority 0 (processed after main)
.RS
Contains: temporary bans, fail2ban jails
.RE

This design ensures whitelisted IPs are never blocked, even if they appear in
threat feeds or fail2ban detections.

.SH PERFORMANCE
.TP
.B Go Binaries (Atomic Operations)
NFTBan includes optimized Go binaries for atomic zero-downtime operations:
.RS
.TP
.I nftban-feeds
Atomic threat feed loader with 5-15x performance improvement.
Features: ETag caching, CIDR merging, delta limiting, ENOBUFS retry.
.TP
.I nftban-geoip
Atomic GeoBan operations via netlink. Country bans in <1 second.
Features: Direct netlink, CPU/RAM monitoring, chunk-based loading.
.RE

.TP
.B Architecture Detection
Wrapper scripts automatically detect architecture (x86_64 or aarch64) and call
the appropriate binary from /usr/lib/nftban/bin/.real/

.TP
.B System Protection (6 Layers)
.RS
.TP
• CPU limit: 80% max (configurable)
.TP
• RAM limit: 4096 MB max (configurable)
.TP
• Chunk size: 4096 IPs per netlink batch
.TP
• Delta limit: 500k IPs max per update
.TP
• ENOBUFS retry: Exponential backoff on kernel buffer full
.TP
• Download limits: 50 MB max, 30s timeout
.RE

.SH SECURITY
.TP
.B FHS Compliance
Strict adherence to Filesystem Hierarchy Standard
.RS
.TP
• /etc/nftban/ - root:root 750 (configs are code-sensitive)
.TP
• /var/lib/nftban/ - nftban:nftban 750 (data isolation)
.TP
• /var/log/nftban/ - nftban:nftban 750 (log privacy)
.RE

.TP
.B Polkit Integration
Two permission levels via group membership:
.RS
.TP
.B nftban-auditors group (READ-ONLY)
View status and generate reports without sudo:
.RS
.TP
• nftban list - View banned IPs
.TP
• nftban stats - View statistics
.TP
• nftban health check - System status
.TP
• CANNOT restart or modify services
.RE
.TP
.B nftban-cli group (FULL MANAGEMENT)
Manage firewall services without sudo:
.RS
.TP
• nftban system restart nftables
.TP
• systemctl start/stop/restart nftables
.TP
• systemctl start/stop/restart fail2ban
.TP
• Scoped permissions (only nftables & fail2ban)
.TP
• Audit trail via systemd journal
.RE
.RE

.TP
.B Audit Logging
All critical operations logged to /var/lib/nftban/audit/permissions.log

.TP
.B SELinux Support
Fully compatible with SELinux in enforcing mode

.SH TIMERS
NFTBan includes systemd timers for automated maintenance:

.TP
.B nftban-main.timer
Weekly maintenance (Sundays at 02:00 AM)
.RS
• Feed updates
.TP
• GeoIP database updates
.TP
• Health checks
.RE

.TP
.B nftban-permissions-audit.timer
Weekly permission audit (Sundays at 02:00 AM)
.RS
• Verify FHS compliance
.TP
• Log any deviations
.TP
• Alert on security issues
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Ban an IP permanently:
.B nftban ban 192.0.2.100 \-\-reason "SSH brute force attack"

.TP
Ban an IP for 1 hour:
.B nftban ban 192.0.2.101 \-\-temp \-\-timeout 3600

.TP
Search for an IP:
.B nftban search 192.0.2.100

.TP
Add to whitelist:
.B nftban whitelist add 203.0.113.50

.TP
Enable and update threat feeds:
.B nftban feeds enable greensnow
.br
.B nftban feeds update

.TP
Ban entire country (GeoBan):
.B nftban geoban ban CN
.br
.B nftban geoban ban RU

.TP
Whitelist a country (never blocked):
.B nftban geoban whitelist US

.TP
List all GeoBan countries:
.B nftban geoban list

.TP
Refresh country IPs:
.B nftban geoban refresh CN

.TP
Lookup IP geolocation:
.B nftban geoip lookup 8.8.8.8

.TP
Bulk lookup from file:
.B nftban geoip bulk ip_list.txt

.TP
Update GeoIP database:
.B nftban geoip update

.TP
Add custom port:
.B nftban port add 8080 tcp

.TP
Search for port:
.B nftban port search 22

.TP
Run health check with auto-healing:
.B nftban health check \-\-auto\-heal

.TP
Generate JSON report:
.B nftban report generate \-\-format json \-\-output /tmp/security-report.json

.TP
Check system statistics:
.B nftban stats \-\-summary

